<P STYLE="text-align: right; margin: 0"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><IMG SRC="tm2415080d1_ex99-1img001.jpg" ALT=""></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>Jaguar Health,&nbsp;Inc. Announces Reverse Stock
Split</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>Reverse split approved at April&nbsp;2024 Special
Meeting of Stockholders</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><I>Shares of Jaguar Health common stock to begin
trading on split-adjusted basis on May&nbsp;23, 2024</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>San Francisco, CA (May&nbsp;17, 2024):</B> <FONT>Jaguar
Health,&nbsp;Inc.</FONT> (<FONT>NASDAQ: JAGX</FONT>) (&ldquo;Jaguar&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;) today
announced that the Company will effect a reverse stock split of its issued and outstanding voting common stock (&ldquo;Common Stock&rdquo;),
at an exchange ratio of 1-for-60, on Thursday, May&nbsp;23, 2024 (the &ldquo;Effective Date&rdquo;) in order to support the Company&rsquo;s
compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s listing standards. The Company&rsquo;s Common Stock will begin trading on a split-adjusted basis when the
market opens on the Effective Date and will remain listed on The Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol &ldquo;JAGX&rdquo;. The new CUSIP
number for the Company&rsquo;s Common Stock following the reverse stock split is 47010C805.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&ldquo;Jaguar&rsquo;s board of directors has determined that effecting
a reverse stock split at this time will, in addition to supporting the Company&rsquo;s compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s listing standards,
provide Jaguar with the opportunity to achieve a share price and outstanding share count that is more attractive to institutional investors,&rdquo;
said Lisa Conte, Jaguar&rsquo;s president and CEO.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">The effectuation of the reverse stock split follows the approval of
a proposal submitted to Jaguar stockholders at a Special Meeting of Stockholders (the &ldquo;Special Meeting&rdquo;). This proposal, which
was approved by the affirmative vote of the holders of a majority in voting power of the votes cast affirmatively or negatively (excluding
abstention and broker non-votes) on such proposal by shares of Jaguar Common Stock and Series&nbsp;J Perpetual Preferred Stock of the
Company outstanding as of the record date for the Special Meeting, is described in detail in the Company&rsquo;s definitive proxy statement
on Schedule 14A relating to the Special Meeting filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (the &ldquo;SEC&rdquo;) on March&nbsp;15,
2024. Stockholders may obtain a free copy of the proxy statement and other documents filed by Jaguar with the SEC at http://www.sec.gov.
The proxy statement is also available on the Company&rsquo;s corporate website.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">When the reverse stock split becomes effective, every sixty (60) shares
of the Company&rsquo;s Common Stock immediately prior to the Effective Date shall automatically be reclassified into one (1)&nbsp;share
of Common Stock, without any change in the par value per share, and this change will be reflected on Nasdaq&rsquo;s website and other
stock quote platforms. No fractional shares will be issued as a result of the reverse stock split. Stockholders who otherwise would be
entitled to receive a fractional share in connection with the reverse stock split will receive a cash payment in lieu thereof.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">Equiniti Trust Company, LLC is acting as exchange agent for the reverse
stock split and will send instructions to stockholders of record who hold stock certificates regarding the exchange of their certificates
for post-reverse stock split shares of Common Stock. Stockholders who hold their shares in brokerage accounts or &ldquo;street name&rdquo;
are not required to take any action to effect the exchange of their shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

